  "meaning": "Conditional stage-2 assembly: for every g satisfying \u03c3.IsGod, derive one, simple, perfect and supremely good from the listed causal and maximality premises, retain the five pointwise attribute premises as inputs, and apply the explicit one-way STMT-CLASSICAL-ATTRIBUTES-SUFFICE to those nine predicates at that same g. HasClassicalAttributes remains a primitive field; no converse or God-existence conclusion follows. Later stage-2 compositions derive the five attribute inputs separately. The bridge is motivated by Dei Filius ch. 1, not asserted by that text as a universal law over arbitrary predicates.",
